DIAG: remoteproc: qcom: scan SMEM for the Q6 crash reason

Temporary, not for upstream.

The Q6 raises its fatal interrupt on every boot and qcom_q6v5 prints
"fatal error without message", meaning SMEM item WCSS_CRASH_REASON (421)
is absent or empty. That may be because the firmware wrote its reason
somewhere else -- multi-PD firmware can use a different item per PD.

Say which of the three cases actually happened, and scan the ids around it
for anything that looks like a message -- in the global partition and in
the WCSS private partition, host 1. qcom_q6v5_mpd.c defines
WCSS_SMEM_HOST for exactly that and never uses it, because mainline's
qcom_q6v5_init() has no way to pass a host through, so the driver only
ever looks in the global partition.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -122,10 +122,51 @@
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	msg = qcom_smem_get(QCOM_SMEM_HOST_ANY, q6v5->crash_reason, &len);
-	if (!IS_ERR(msg) && len > 0 && msg[0])
+	if (!IS_ERR(msg) && len > 0 && msg[0]) {
 		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "fatal error received: %s\n", msg);
-	else
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "fatal error without message\n");
+	} else {
+		static const int diag_ids[] = {
+			421, 422, 423, 424, 425, 426, 427, 428,
+			429, 430, 431, 432, 433, 434, 435, 436,
+			134, 135, 136, 137, 138, 139,
+		};
+		int i;
+
+		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "fatal error without message (id %d: %s)\n",
+			q6v5->crash_reason,
+			IS_ERR(msg) ? "absent" : (len ? "empty string" : "zero length"));
+
+		/* DIAG: the Q6 may have written its reason under a different
+		 * SMEM item than the one this driver asks for. Scan the ids
+		 * around it and report anything that looks like a message.
+		 */
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(diag_ids); i++) {
+			size_t l;
+			char *m;
+			int h;
+
+			/* Host -1 reads the global partition only. The
+			 * downstream driver this was derived from read the
+			 * crash reason out of the WCSS private partition,
+			 * host 1 -- qcom_q6v5_mpd.c even defines
+			 * WCSS_SMEM_HOST for it and then never uses it,
+			 * because mainline's qcom_q6v5_init() has no way to
+			 * pass a host through. Try both.
+			 */
+			for (h = 0; h < 2; h++) {
+				int host = h ? 1 : QCOM_SMEM_HOST_ANY;
+
+				m = qcom_smem_get(host, diag_ids[i], &l);
+				if (IS_ERR(m) || !l)
+					continue;
+				dev_err(q6v5->dev, "DIAG smem[host %d, id %d] len=%zu first=%02x %02x %02x %02x: %.96s\n",
+					host, diag_ids[i], l,
+					(u8)m[0], l > 1 ? (u8)m[1] : 0,
+					l > 2 ? (u8)m[2] : 0, l > 3 ? (u8)m[3] : 0,
+					m[0] ? m : "(starts with NUL)");
+			}
+		}
+	}
 
 	q6v5->running = false;
 	rproc_report_crash(q6v5->rproc, RPROC_FATAL_ERROR);
